---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import RedactScannedDocument from '@/components/tools/redact/scan/RedactScannedDocument.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="redact-scanned-document" width="wide">
  <RedactScannedDocument client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to redact a scanned document</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Drop a scanned PDF, or photos or scans of pages as JPG or PNG.</li>
      <li>Each page is read with OCR. Names, addresses, emails, phone, card and account numbers, dates and ID numbers get a black box.</li>
      <li>Click a box to keep that text visible. Drag on the page to cover anything else.</li>
      <li>Choose what to hide, and add words to the always-hide list. The boxes change at once.</li>
      <li>Download a PDF, or the pages as PNG or JPG images.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The OCR engine (Tesseract with its English data, about 7 MB) reads the words and where they are on the page. Pattern
      rules check the text for emails, phone numbers, card numbers with the Luhn check, IBANs with the mod 97 check, dates
      and national ID numbers. A small language model (21 MB, with a 15 MB runtime) finds names, places and addresses. These
      files download once from this site and stay in your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each page of the PDF is saved as an image with the boxes burned in. No text layer is kept, so nothing under a box can
      be copied out.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open your browser's developer tools, select the Network tab and drop a file. You see the OCR engine and the model load
      from this site the first time, and no request after that.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>OCR needs a sharp, straight page. Blurry photos, handwriting and very small print are read badly or not at all, and then nothing is found there.</li>
      <li>The OCR data is English. Other languages in Latin script are read with more mistakes.</li>
      <li>Each page takes a few seconds. Look at every page before you share the result.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
